   Added: Expand all / Collapse all ButtonControls on the grid's ExpandAllAsync / CollapseAllAsync. Height="100%" became the 440px
   the wrapper gave it. Parameter tables are a later pass (SC-278). *@

<PageTitle>Tree grid — FlexCore Showcase</PageTitle>

<FeatureDemoLayout Title="Tree grid" Category="Data Grid" CategoryHref="demo/grid" ControlName="TreeGridControl"
                   Tagline="A flat list with Id and ParentId columns, shown as a collapsible hierarchy."
                   SourcePath="Grid/TreeGridControl.razor;Grid/TreeGridControl.razor.cs;Grid/TreeGridColumn.cs">
    <Overview>
        <p>
            <code>TreeGridControl</code> builds the hierarchy from two property names on a flat list: <code>IdMapping</code> names the key and
            <code>ParentIdMapping</code> the parent key, null or empty for a root. <code>TreatAsParent</code> marks rows as expandable even
            before their children are in the list, <code>TreeColumnIndex</code> picks the column that carries the indentation and icons, <code>NodeExpandIconStyle</code> is
            <code>PlusMinus</code> or <code>Triangle</code>, <code>EnableCollapseAll</code> starts with every node collapsed, and
            <code>ToggleOnRowClick="false"</code> limits toggling to the icon. <code>Expanded</code> and <code>Collapsed</code> report the node
            and its level; <code>ExpandAllAsync</code> and <code>CollapseAllAsync</code> do the same from code.
        </p>
    </Overview>

    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Id="tree" Title="Divisions and their phases" RazorCode="@Code.Tree" CSharpCode="@Code.TreeCs">
            <Description><p>Each division is a root row and its phases are children, all in one flat list. Click a plus to open a division, or use Expand all. Change the size to rebuild the list with more divisions and phases; the line under the grid counts the rows the grid received and names the last node you opened or closed.</p></Description>
            <Controls>
                <ButtonGroupControl Items="_sizes" Values="@(new[] { _groupCount.ToString() })"
                                    ValuesChanged="@(v => SetScale(v.Count > 0 ? int.Parse(v[0]) : 10))"
                                    Selection="ChoiceSelectionMode.Single" AriaLabel="Tree size" />
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _tree?.ExpandAllAsync() ?? Task.CompletedTask)">Expand all</ButtonControl>
                <ButtonControl CssClass="btn-sm" OnClick="@(() => _tree?.CollapseAllAsync() ?? Task.CompletedTask)">Collapse all</ButtonControl>
            </Controls>
            <Demo>
                <TreeGridControl @ref="_tree"
                                 @key="_treeGeneration"
                                 TValue="BenchTreeNode"
                                 DataSource="@_treeNodes"
                                 IdMapping="NodeID"
                                 ParentIdMapping="ParentID"
                                 TreeColumnIndex="0"
                                 EnableCollapseAll="true"
                                 AllowSelection="true"
                                 ToggleOnRowClick="false"
                                 Height="440px"
                                 CssClass="fx-treegrid-compact fx-treegrid-yellow-folder fx-treegrid-dotted-lines"
                                 NodeExpandIconStyle="GroupExpandIconStyle.PlusMinus"
                                 TreatAsParent="TreatAsParent"
                                 Expanded="@(a => _last = $"opened {a.Data?.Node} (level {a.Level})")"
                                 Collapsed="@(a => _last = $"closed {a.Data?.Node} (level {a.Level})")">
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="Node" HeaderText="Division and phase" Width="380px" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="PhaseCount" HeaderText="Phases" Width="90px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Center" />
                    <TreeGridColumn Field="Budget" HeaderText="Budget" Width="140px" TextAlign="TextAlign.Right" Format="$#,##0.00" />
                </TreeGridControl>
                <p class="result">@_treeNodes.Count rows: @_groupCount divisions with @_phasesPerGroup phases each@(_last is null ? "" : $" · last {_last}")</p>
            </Demo>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>

    <Vocabulary>
        <p class="fd-pending"><code>TreeGridControl</code> (92 parameters), <code>TreeGridColumn</code> and <code>TreeNodeEventArgs</code> are still to be written up from <code>Grid/TreeGridControl.razor.cs</code> and <code>Grid/TreeGridColumn.cs</code>.</p>
    </Vocabulary>

    <Related>
        <ul>
            <li><a href="demo/tree/treeview-explorer">Tree view</a>: a hierarchy without columns.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid/grouping">Grouping &amp; totals</a>: a flat grid folded by a column value instead of a parent key.</li>
            <li><a href="demo/grid">Grid overview</a>: the core flags on a small list.</li>
        </ul>
    </Related>
</FeatureDemoLayout>

@code {
    private readonly SelectionItem[] _sizes = { new("10", "Small"), new("30", "Medium"), new("60", "Large") };
    private TreeGridControl<BenchTreeNode>? _tree;
    private List<BenchTreeNode> _treeNodes = [];
    private int _groupCount = 10;
    private int _phasesPerGroup = 4;
    private int _treeGeneration = 1;   // @key: a new value remounts the tree grid when the list is rebuilt
    private string? _last;

    protected override void OnInitialized()
    {
        GenerateTree();
    }

    private void SetScale(int groups)
    {
        _groupCount = groups;
        _phasesPerGroup = groups switch { 30 => 6, 60 => 8, _ => 4 };
        _last = null;
        GenerateTree();
    }

    private void GenerateTree()
    {
        var list = new List<BenchTreeNode>();
        var rand = new Random(33);

        var groupTitles = new[]
        {
            "0100 - General Requirements",
            "0200 - Existing Site Conditions",
            "0300 - Concrete Foundations",
            "0400 - Masonry & Stonework",
            "0500 - Metals & Structural Steel",
            "0600 - Wood, Plastics & Composites",
            "0700 - Thermal & Moisture Protection",
            "0800 - Openings (Doors & Windows)",
            "0900 - Finishes & Drywall",
            "1000 - Specialties & Accessories"
        };

        for (int g = 1; g <= _groupCount; g++)
        {
            var gId = $"G-{g:D3}";
            var gTitle = groupTitles[(g - 1) % groupTitles.Length];
            decimal groupBudget = 0;

            var childNodes = new List<BenchTreeNode>();
            for (int p = 1; p <= _phasesPerGroup; p++)
            {
                var pBudget = Math.Round((decimal)(rand.NextDouble() * 35000 + 5000), 2);
                groupBudget += pBudget;
                childNodes.Add(new BenchTreeNode
                {
                    NodeID = $"P-{g:D3}-{p:D2}",
                    ParentID = gId,
                    Node = $"Phase {p}",
                    Level = 2,
                    IsGroup = false,
                    PhaseCount = 1,
                    Budget = pBudget
                });
            }

            list.Add(new BenchTreeNode
            {
                NodeID = gId,
                ParentID = null,
                Node = $"{gTitle} (Division {g})",
                Level = 1,
                IsGroup = true,
                PhaseCount = _phasesPerGroup,
                Budget = groupBudget
            });

            list.AddRange(childNodes);
        }

        _treeNodes = list;
        _treeGeneration++;
    }

    private bool TreatAsParent(BenchTreeNode node) => node.IsGroup;

    // Code tabs are verbatim copies of the Demo block and the members above (generated, not typed); the C# tab also carries
    // BenchTreeNode from Data/BenchModels.cs.
    private static class Code
    {
        public const string Tree = @"<TreeGridControl @ref=""_tree""
                 @key=""_treeGeneration""
                 TValue=""BenchTreeNode""
                 DataSource=""@_treeNodes""
                 IdMapping=""NodeID""
                 ParentIdMapping=""ParentID""
                 TreeColumnIndex=""0""
                 EnableCollapseAll=""true""
                 AllowSelection=""true""
                 ToggleOnRowClick=""false""
                 Height=""440px""
                 CssClass=""fx-treegrid-compact fx-treegrid-yellow-folder fx-treegrid-dotted-lines""
                 NodeExpandIconStyle=""GroupExpandIconStyle.PlusMinus""
                 TreatAsParent=""TreatAsParent""
                 Expanded=""@(a => _last = $""opened {a.Data?.Node} (level {a.Level})"")""
                 Collapsed=""@(a => _last = $""closed {a.Data?.Node} (level {a.Level})"")"">
    <TreeGridColumn Field=""Node"" HeaderText=""Division and phase"" Width=""380px"" />
    <TreeGridColumn Field=""PhaseCount"" HeaderText=""Phases"" Width=""90px"" TextAlign=""TextAlign.Center"" />
    <TreeGridColumn Field=""Budget"" HeaderText=""Budget"" Width=""140px"" TextAlign=""TextAlign.Right"" Format=""$#,##0.00"" />
</TreeGridControl>
<p class=""result"">@_treeNodes.Count rows: @_groupCount divisions with @_phasesPerGroup phases each@(_last is null ? """" : $"" · last {_last}"")</p>";
        public const string TreeCs = @"private readonly SelectionItem[] _sizes = { new(""10"", ""Small""), new(""30"", ""Medium""), new(""60"", ""Large"") };

private TreeGridControl<BenchTreeNode>? _tree;

private List<BenchTreeNode> _treeNodes = [];

